two recorded differences and no third. cl inlines the closures away and emits no symbol for their call operators where cxx1 emits real functions, having no COMDAT - the difference lambda.nocl records. And cl emits ??_R0H@8, the type descriptor a Microsoft throw is identified by, which condition-declaration-unwind.nocl already records for the case with a try in it; this one has a try of its own, in the function that holds a lambda inside it. What the case is for - the eight pieces of per-function state a nested parse has to put back - is checked by run-cases.cmd on the box and run.sh on the other two, and by the ledger line in its .expected.
